title: 'pallet-recovery: fix try_state check 5b for zero security deposit'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Check 5b in `do_try_state` previously required a nonzero `SecurityDeposit` hold
    unconditionally. `MigrateV0ToV1` deliberately stores zero when it cannot hold the
    deposit for the rescuer; `cancel_attempt` and `approve_attempt` release via
    `Precision::BestEffort`, so that state is consistent.

    The check now compares the hold against the stored deposit instead of against zero.
    A zero stored deposit with zero hold passes. A nonzero stored deposit with a shortfall
    still fails. This unblocks `try-runtime` checks against Asset Hub Kusama, where nine
    of fourteen `Attempt` entries were inserted by the migration with a zero deposit.

crates:
- name: pallet-recovery
  bump: patch
